    "lede": "Core exposes a small reusable cache scope. The TypeScript service takes less input at turn start and returns an awaitable release.",
    "body": "\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Public surface</th><th>Before</th><th>After</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Core export</td><td>No turn-cache abstraction</td><td><code>TurnScopedCacheScope</code> and <code>TurnScopedCache&lt;Key, Value&gt;</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Service beginTurn</td><td><code>(snapshot: WorkspaceSnapshot): void</code></td><td><code>(files: readonly WorkspaceFile[]): void</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Service release</td><td><code>(): void</code></td><td><code>(): Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Backend release</td><td><code>(): Promise&lt;void&gt;</code><br>project promise detached</td><td><code>(): Promise&lt;void&gt;</code><br>project promise awaited</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"two-up\">\n <figure class=\"diagram\"><figcaption class=\"diagram-title\">What a query gets</figcaption><div class=\"unit changed\"><strong>TurnScopedCache&lt;Key, Value&gt;</strong><code>getOrCreate(key, createValue): Value</code></div><p class=\"caption\">A typed handle. The public interface does not expose its internal clear method.</p></figure>\n <figure class=\"diagram\"><figcaption class=\"diagram-title\">What the lifetime owner gets</figcaption><div class=\"unit changed\"><strong>TurnScopedCacheScope</strong><code>createCache&lt;Key, Value&gt;()</code><br><code>beginTurn(): void</code><br><code>releaseTransientResources(): void</code></div><p class=\"caption\">All handles register here. Both lifecycle methods clear their values together.</p></figure>\n</div>\n<div class=\"reasons\">\n<div class=\"reason\"><span class=\"badge unexplained\">D8 · unexplained</span>\n    <div><strong>Accept just the file list at beginTurn.</strong><p>The old service already read only snapshot.files, and the backend now passes request.snapshot.files. That explains the mechanical fit, not the author's reason for changing the exported signature; no reason for the narrowing was found.</p>\n    <a href=\"#e-surface\" data-go=\"e-surface\">Before/after signatures and call site →</a></div></div><div class=\"reason\"><span class=\"badge unexplained\">D9 · unexplained</span>\n    <div><strong>Expose only factory lookup and whole-scope reset.</strong><p>No per-key invalidation, cancellation, timer, phase token, or unregister/dispose method is exported. Handles persist through clears. The source makes those limits visible; the available rationale does not compare this surface with a richer one.</p>\n    <a href=\"#e-surface\" data-go=\"e-surface\">Complete core interface and implementation →</a></div></div></div><p class=\"small\">The new core export follows the stated ownership move (D1). The asynchronous service release follows the stated completion barrier (D6). Neither requires a new internal package dependency direction.</p>",
